  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Biosecurity Engagement Program (BEP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On November 12, 2012 APHIS Bangkok attended the opening ceremony of the training which was funded through the Dept. of State Biological Engagement Program. There were 15 participants from 14 countries including Burma, Cambodia, Indonesia, Philippines, Thailand, Sri Lanka, Nepal, Pakistan, Egypt, Mongolia, Ethiopia, Senegal, Samoa and Suriname. The instructors were from CU, Department of Livestock Development, Ministry of Public Health, US-CDC and US Armed Forces Research Institute of Medical Sciences (AFRIMS).</narrative>
  </description>
